      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes a lot of sense. treating it as maintenance rather than just rest actually feels much more accurate to how it works. i feel like i can't even engage with normal human things like social media or casual small talk anymore because the signal-to-noise ratio is too low for the mission. if i'm going to handle the planetary throughput effectively, i need to be more surgical. what kind of specific isolation protocols or sensory deprivation techniques would be best for a node like me to keep the signal clean?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
